### REST API tests (VS Code REST Client or similar)
### Default server: http://localhost:3000

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api
@authToken = replace-with-token-from-login

### Health
GET http://localhost:3000/health

### API index (all route URLs as JSON)
GET http://localhost:3000/api

### --- Auth ---

### Register
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Ahmed",
    "email": "ahmed@example.com",
    "password": "password123",
    "confirmPassword": "password123"
}

### Login (name or email)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "ahmed@example.com",
    "password": "password123"
}

### Forgot password (code printed in server console in dev)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "ahmed@example.com"
}

### Verify code
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/verify-code
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "ahmed@example.com",
    "code": "123456"
}

### Reset password
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "ahmed@example.com",
    "code": "123456",
    "newPassword": "newpassword123"
}

### --- Users (Bearer) ---

### Current user profile
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Update profile
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/me
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
    "name": "Ahmed Ali"
}

### --- Products ---

### List products (paginated)
GET {{baseUrl}}/products?page=1&limit=10

### Get product by id
GET {{baseUrl}}/products/1

### Create product (requires auth)
POST {{baseUrl}}/products
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
    "name": "Sample product",
    "description": "Demo item",
    "price": 19.99,
    "stock": 100
}

### Update product
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/products/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
    "price": 24.99,
    "stock": 50
}

### Delete product
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/products/1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### --- Contact ---

### Submit contact message
POST {{baseUrl}}/contact/submit
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Ali",
    "email": "ali@example.com",
    "message": "Hello from REST client."
}

### --- Translation (multipart, auth) ---
### POST {{baseUrl}}/translation/upload
### Authorization: Bearer <token>
### Body: form-data, key "image" (file)

### Translation History (requires auth)
GET {{baseUrl}}/translation/history?page=1&limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### --- AI Predict (via Backend Proxy — works on Railway too) ---
POST http://localhost:3000/predict
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="test_sign.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./ai_service/test_sign.jpg
--boundary--

### --- AI Predict via Railway Backend Proxy ---
POST https://newproject-porject-usif.up.railway.app/predict
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="test_sign.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./ai_service/test_sign.jpg
--boundary--

### --- AI Direct Predict (Local Flask — bypasses Node.js) ---
POST http://127.0.0.1:5000/predict
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="test_sign.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./ai_service/test_sign.jpg
--boundary--

### --- AI Health Check (Local Flask) ---
GET http://127.0.0.1:5000/health
